296
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:26,620
我们会把要做的事情拆成一块一块的工作单元
We have chunks of work that we want to do,

297
00:20:26,760 --> 00:20:28,180
比如我们想给应用加的功能
features we want to add to our apps,

298
00:20:28,320 --> 00:20:29,840
我们想要做的可靠性相关工作
reliability work that we want to do.

299
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:32,320
我们把那张工单交给一个智能体
We give that ticket to an agent,

300
00:20:32,420 --> 00:20:36,700
同时再给它配上几项能让它操作我们应用的技能
along with a couple of skills that enable it to manipulate our app.

301
00:20:37,580 --> 00:20:40,880
我们希望开发流程的入口是Codex
We want the entry point to the development process to be Codex,

302
00:20:40,980 --> 00:20:43,660
而不是我们在它周围搭建的某个环境
not an environment which we build around it.

303
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:48,060
所以我们有点像是从外向里地做事对吧
So, we kind of do things outside-in, right?

304
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:50,700
Codex 是入口点，就像你本来也会是一样
Codex is the entry point, the same way you would be,

305
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:51,820
我们给它提供工具
and we give it tools,

306
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:53,400
我们给它提供“怎么下厨”的指令
we give it instructions on how to cook.

307
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:58,160
所以我们不是创建一个壳把我们的应用和Codex一起塞进去
So, rather than creating a shell that our app and Codex get spawned into,

308
00:20:58,640 --> 00:21:01,060
而是提供一个技能教Codex如何启动应用
we have a skill that teaches Codex how to launch the app,

309
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:05,860
教Codex如何拉起本地可观测性栈来提供日志和遥测
that teaches Codex how to spin up that local observability stack to give it logging and telemetry.

310
00:21:06,300 --> 00:21:13,000
我们给它一个技能让它能启动Chrome DevTools并附加到
We give it a skill that enables it to boot up Chrome DevTools and attach to the

311
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:18,460
应用上去 通过一个本地CLI连接到我们运行的某个守护进程
application with a local CLI that will connect via some daemon that we have.

312
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:24,280
所以我们设置代码仓库以及所有本地开发工具的整个方式
So, the whole way we have set up the repository and all of the local DevTools is for

313
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:25,720
就是为了让Codex先来调用它们
Codex to invoke them first.

314
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:31,000
这意味着我们在代码库里有一堆小型的迷你“驾驭器”
That means we have kind of like a bunch of little mini-harnesses within the codebase that

315
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:33,920
让我们可以很容易地插入额外的护栏
make it really easy for us to slot in additional guardrails.

316
00:21:34,900 --> 00:21:41,180
比如一大包自定义ESLint规则 会被接入工作区里每一个pnpm包
You know, a big package of custom ESLint rules which get wired into every pnpm package in the workspace.

317
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:47,260
我们还有另一种本地开发驾驭器 让我们可以添加更高层次的
We have another sort of local dev harness that allows us to add sort of like higher level

318
00:21:47,260 --> 00:21:52,940
整体性测试 去断言代码本身的结构 而不是只看
holistic tests that assert the structure of the code itself rather than like either the

319
00:21:52,940 --> 00:21:54,740
语法或代码行为
syntax or the behavior of the code.

320
00:21:55,140 --> 00:21:56,460
比如说
Things like, you know,

321
00:21:57,620 --> 00:22:01,620
包的私有性 我们技术栈不同层之间的依赖边界
package privacy, dependency edges between different layers of our stack,

322
00:22:01,720 --> 00:22:02,440
诸如此类的东西
these sorts of things.

323
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:06,680
确保在多个文件之间
Making sure that, you know, across multiple files,

324
00:22:06,820 --> 00:22:08,240
Zod的schema不会重复定义
Zod schemas are deduplicated,

325
00:22:08,400 --> 00:22:11,880
确保我们的异步辅助函数只有一个规范实现
that there's a single canonical implementation of like our async helpers,

326
00:22:12,420 --> 00:22:13,360
之类的事情
these sorts of things.

327
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:19,100
因为我们观察到智能体有时会倾向于优化某个包的局部
Because, you know, the way we have seen the agents work is to sometimes optimize for local

328
00:22:19,100 --> 00:22:24,580
一致性 而不是去用我们的共享工具库之类的东西
coherence of a package rather than using like our shared utilities and things like that.

329
00:22:24,780 --> 00:22:26,140
所以在观察到这种行为之后
So having observed that behavior,

330
00:22:26,440 --> 00:22:32,300
我们就构建了一堆伪代码检查（lint）式的源码校验工具
we kind of have built a bunch of little pseudo-linter source code verification things that

331
00:22:32,300 --> 00:22:37,380
把这些不良行为筛出来 这样人类在代码评审时就不用被这些问题分心
shake out some of that bad behavior so the humans don't get distracted paying attention to that in reviews.

332
00:22:37,780 --> 00:22:46,000
大致就是这些 但整个设置是为了让智能体来完成工作 而人类不必去追踪
Stuff like that. But the setup optimizes for the agent to do the job and for the humans to not have to keep

333
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:47,840
代码库里那些高频变动
track of the high churn in the code base.

334
00:22:48,620 --> 00:22:52,280
我们基本把杠杆集中在五到十个技能上
We kind of centralize our leverage around 5 to 10 skills.

335
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:55,080
我们不会在技能数量上铺得特别开
We don't go super wide on skills,

336
00:22:55,180 --> 00:22:57,640
而是更倾向于把现有技能打磨得更好
preferring to make the existing skills better.

337
00:22:58,160 --> 00:23:03,540
因为至少在我看来 仓库里的基础设施
Because at least I find that the infrastructure within the repository,

338
00:23:03,740 --> 00:23:06,420
以及所有本地开发工具变化都非常频繁
all the local developer tools change super frequently.

339
00:23:06,980 --> 00:23:10,000
而我其实没有精力去追踪这些变化
And I don't really have the bandwidth to keep track of this.

340
00:23:10,120 --> 00:23:16,320
所以我们把这些复杂度都藏在那些人类需要调用的技能下面
So we hide all that complexity beneath the skills that the human has to invoke and let the

341
00:23:16,320 --> 00:23:17,520
让智能体自己去搞定
agent just kind of figure it out.

342
00:23:17,920 --> 00:23:24,280
有个挺有意思的例子是 当我们从直接使用Chrome DevTools协议
One kind of neat thing here is when we moved from using Chrome DevTools protocol directly

343
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:25,860
迁移到用这么一个守护进程方案时
to having this like daemon thing,

344
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,420
我有大概三周时间都不知道这事已经发生了
I didn't know that had happened for like three weeks.

345
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:32,000
但一切都完全没问题 因为Codex照样能完成任务
It was like totally fine because Codex was able to do the thing,

346
00:23:32,040 --> 00:23:35,020
靠的就是我们已有的文档和相关内容
you know, with the documentation and things that we had in place.

347
00:23:35,720 --> 00:23:38,080
其中一部分内容 你可以在你的文章里看到更详细的说明
And part of this, you can get more detail in your article.

