00:23:44,980 --> 00:23:48,060
是要搞上千个技能 还是把它简化成少数几个
thousands of skills versus simplifying it to just quite a few.

351
00:23:48,440 --> 00:23:54,660
好 那继续说 你是怎么避免自己在驾驭器上过度设计的
But okay. Continuing on, how do you stop yourself from overengineering harnesses?

352
00:23:54,840 --> 00:24:01,260
还有个类似的追问是 你会经常给自己做一些小工具吗 如果会的话
And a little bit of a similar follow up is do you often build small tools for yourself, if ever?

353
00:24:01,900 --> 00:24:03,240
你会做定制工具吗
Do you build custom tools?

354
00:24:03,860 --> 00:24:08,500
会的 我觉得这其实有点在指向所谓“苦涩教训”对吧
Yeah. So I think this is kind of gesturing in the direction of the bitter lesson here, right?

355
00:24:08,560 --> 00:24:13,760
也就是我要如何确保我做的工作不会因为
Which is how do I make sure the work that I do isn't like completely obsoleted by an

356
00:24:13,760 --> 00:24:15,080
模型能力的提升而被完全淘汰
increase in model capability?

357
00:24:15,520 --> 00:24:21,080
而我对这件事的思考是 只做最低限度的上下文
And the way I have thought about that is doing sort of the bare minimum amount of context

358
00:24:21,080 --> 00:24:27,460
管理 把智能体在整个工作过程中
management to kind of pull in requirements for the agent to do an acceptable job over the

359
00:24:27,460 --> 00:24:28,220
做到“合格”所需要的需求拉进来
course of its work.

360
00:24:28,860 --> 00:24:32,860
而上下文本身这件事 我觉得是永远不会被淘汰的对吧
And context is a thing that I don't think will ever be obsoleted, right?

361
00:24:32,960 --> 00:24:34,780
模型必须被告知
The models must be told,

362
00:24:34,860 --> 00:24:37,060
比如任务的需求
like, the requirements of the task,

363
00:24:37,180 --> 00:24:38,740
要注意哪些护栏
which guardrails to pay attention to,

364
00:24:38,840 --> 00:24:39,680
诸如此类的信息
these sorts of things.

365
00:24:40,280 --> 00:24:46,140
所以一个好的驾驭器 其实就是围绕在正确的时间把文本给到模型来运作
So a good harness is really operationalized around giving the model text at the right time

366
00:24:46,140 --> 00:24:50,820
这样它就能对照自己已经做的工作和“什么叫做好”的相关信息
so it can look at the work it has done and the information around what a good job looks like.

367
00:24:51,460 --> 00:24:55,820
而且从根本上说 模型是被训练来遵循指令的
And, you know, fundamentally the models are trained to follow instructions.

368
00:24:56,240 --> 00:25:00,080
驾驭器要做的就是在正确的时间把指令呈现给模型
All the harness should do is surface instructions to the model at the right time.

369
00:25:00,780 --> 00:25:03,640
所以我们也希望把这个量降到最小对吧
So we do want to minimize that, too, right?

370
00:25:03,640 --> 00:25:06,740
你不想一开始就把所有指令都塞给它 不然你就会
You don't want to front load all those instructions because then you kind of,

371
00:25:06,760 --> 00:25:08,300
把智能体给“喂爆”
like, overwhelm the agent.

372
00:25:08,640 --> 00:25:13,040
但所有关于“什么叫做好”的这些要求
But all of these sort of requirements around what a good job do need to be paid attention

373
00:25:13,040 --> 00:25:15,020
都需要在整个PR生命周期里被持续关注 对吧
to over the entire course of the PR, right?

374
00:25:15,240 --> 00:25:21,440
所以想办法要么延后 要么在恰当时机再把这些指令抛出来
So figuring out ways to either defer or just in time surface those instructions is kind of

375
00:25:21,440 --> 00:25:23,920
这基本就是一个好驾驭器该做的事对吧
what a good harness should do, right?

376
00:25:24,620 --> 00:25:29,900
比如你知道自己希望React组件
If you know that you want your React components,

377
00:25:30,040 --> 00:25:35,180
被拆分成更无状态的小块 以便做出好的快照测试 对吧
right, to be decomposed so that they make good snapshot tests for individual more stateless pieces, right?

378
00:25:35,360 --> 00:25:37,120
你没必要一开始就把这个要求塞进去
You don't need to load that up front.

379
00:25:37,520 --> 00:25:41,220
相反 你应该先让智能体自由发挥 去做原型 去尝试你想要构建的UI
Instead, you should kind of let the agent cook and prototype and experiment with the UI

380
00:25:41,220 --> 00:25:41,900
也就是你想要构建的界面
you want to build.

381
00:25:42,260 --> 00:25:43,880
然后在代码检查（lint）或测试阶段
And then at lint or test time,

382
00:25:43,980 --> 00:25:45,920
再告诉它 好 你已经把功能写完了
say, okay, you've done the work.

383
00:25:45,960 --> 00:25:46,940
为了把这事真正收尾
In order to finish it,

384
00:25:46,980 --> 00:25:50,620
你得把这些东西拆开 让组件变得更小 更无状态
you have to break this apart so that your components are small and as stateless as

385
00:25:50,620 --> 00:25:54,900
并且通过本地hooks依赖而不是一层层传props 或者任何你希望代码呈现的样子
possible and have local dependencies on hooks instead of prop drilling or whatever it is

386
00:25:54,900 --> 00:25:56,920
也就是你希望代码呈现出来的结构
that you want the code to look like.

387
00:25:57,180 --> 00:25:58,200
然后智能体就会“意识到”
And then the agent will say,

388
00:25:58,300 --> 00:26:00,260
哦 这是一个新的指令
oh, this is a new instruction for me.

389
00:26:00,440 --> 00:26:01,760
让我基于已经写好的补丁
Let me take the patch as written,

390
00:26:02,240 --> 00:26:04,380
做修改以确保它符合这些指令
modify it to make sure that it adheres to the instructions,

391
00:26:04,700 --> 00:26:06,280
然后把它推到GitHub上去
and then up it goes to GitHub.

392
00:26:06,860 --> 00:26:11,880
而这种东西不会因为模型能力的提升而被淘汰
And this sort of thing is not going to be obsoleted by increases in model capability.

393
00:26:12,100 --> 00:26:14,640
它本质上就是要拿到那段正确的文本
It's really just about getting that right text,

394
00:26:14,760 --> 00:26:16,520
在正确的时间提供正确的上下文
that right context at the right time.

395
00:26:17,580 --> 00:26:20,220
我们能不能聊一个好的驾驭器的例子
