00:43:21,380 --> 00:43:26,200
从宏观层面上，你能给我们描绘一下你正在构建的未来图景吗
At a high level, can you give us a picture of what future you're building for?

682
00:43:26,520 --> 00:43:27,720
到那时上下文还重要吗
Does context still matter?

683
00:43:28,140 --> 00:43:30,100
人们会如何做工程
How do people do engineering,

684
00:43:30,300 --> 00:43:31,680
如何做驾驭式工程、上下文工程
harness engineering, context engineering?

685
00:43:32,000 --> 00:43:33,140
未来会是什么样子
What does the future look like?

686
00:43:35,380 --> 00:43:42,200
我想要构建的未来，大致是这样的：我可以拿出一个Token预算
Sort of the future that I want to build toward here is where I'm able to take a token

687
00:43:42,200 --> 00:43:46,040
再加上一个季度
budget and a quarter,

688
00:43:46,540 --> 00:43:53,320
半年，或者一年的工作量，然后用人类输入来排序什么最重要
a half, or a year's worth of work and take the human input to rank what is most important,

689
00:43:53,780 --> 00:43:56,280
包括成功指标、可靠性指标
success metrics, reliability metrics,

690
00:43:56,660 --> 00:43:57,860
把这些交给机器
give it to the machines,

691
00:43:58,160 --> 00:44:04,140
让它们持续工作，不断推动我的产品向前发展，而不需要我亲自下场
and have them continually work and advance my product forward without sort of my hands

692
00:44:04,140 --> 00:44:05,680
完全不需要亲自上手操作键盘鼠标
explicitly on the wheels at all.

693
00:44:07,600 --> 00:44:12,580
随着我们从非常早期的原型阶段一路走到内部 Alpha
As we have gone through very early prototyping to internal alpha,

694
00:44:13,440 --> 00:44:15,480
内部 Beta，再到外部 Alpha
internal beta, external alpha,

695
00:44:15,480 --> 00:44:20,740
我逐渐感觉到，软件工程流程中的一些新环节好像
I kind of have felt that new parts of the software engineering process have kind of

696
00:44:20,740 --> 00:44:23,540
是从零开始的，我们不得不一点点把能力搭建起来
started from zero and we've had to build up capability.

697
00:44:23,820 --> 00:44:30,500
有点像那种五边形性格雷达图，在某个方向我能力值拉得很高
Kind of like these pentagonal personality charts where I spike in this direction,

698
00:44:30,660 --> 00:44:32,000
但在另一些方向我可能就比较薄弱
maybe I'm weak over here.

699
00:44:32,540 --> 00:44:36,360
当我们第一次走到真正部署软件这一步时
And when we get to deployed software for the first time,

700
00:44:36,900 --> 00:44:42,580
在构建产物被提升到发布阶段之前，智能体对这些产物做冒烟测试的能力
the agent's ability to do QA smoke testing on our built artifacts before they're promoted

701
00:44:42,580 --> 00:44:44,060
是很薄弱的
to distribution was weak.

702
00:44:44,200 --> 00:44:45,620
我们之前完全没在这方面投入时间
We hadn't invested any time in this.

703
00:44:45,720 --> 00:44:49,740
没有文档，也没有工具让智能体可以下载构建产物
There were no docs, there were no tools that the agents could use to download the built

704
00:44:49,740 --> 00:44:54,940
启动它、到处点点看，来确保我们最关键的用户路径
artifact, launch it, poke around to make sure that our most critical user journeys were

705
00:44:54,940 --> 00:44:56,280
得到了充分的验证和测试
well validated and tested.

706
00:44:56,980 --> 00:44:59,700
所以因为我不想亲自碰电脑
So because I don't want to be touching the computer,

707
00:45:00,420 --> 00:45:04,740
我们就得想办法让智能体自己构建工具来完成这部分工作
we needed to figure out ways for the agents to build themselves tools to do that part.

708
00:45:05,720 --> 00:45:10,840
而在写代码之外，还有整整一个软件工程的宇宙
And there's a whole universe of software engineering outside of writing code.

709
00:45:11,080 --> 00:45:12,920
我在分拣用户反馈
I'm triaging user feedback,

710
00:45:13,260 --> 00:45:20,380
我在处理告警页面，确保线上日志里没有任何个人敏感信息泄露
I'm triaging pages, I'm making sure that we don't have any PII leaking in the logs in production.

711
00:45:20,860 --> 00:45:25,140
我在关注 Twitter 上的舆论氛围，确认大家在享受使用我的软件
I'm making sure that the Twitter vibes are good and people are enjoying my software.

712
00:45:25,820 --> 00:45:31,640
我还要确保用户运营团队有写得很好的操作手册支撑他们
That our user operations staff are supported with well-written run books that allow them

713
00:45:31,640 --> 00:45:34,960
去分级处理并缓解高频用户问题
to triage and mitigate high-volume user issues.

714
00:45:35,140 --> 00:45:38,140
然后再把这些经验落实回代码里，从源头上避免这些问题发生
And then moving that into the code itself so they don't happen in the first place.

715
00:45:38,800 --> 00:45:41,920
而当我不再需要亲自写代码时
And as I no longer have to produce code,

716
00:45:42,660 --> 00:45:47,060
我的精力就可以转向这些更高层次、也更偏软性的活动
my mind can shift to these other higher-level or more squishy activities,

717
00:45:47,320 --> 00:45:49,580
但智能体其实也已经足够胜任这些事情
but the agents are good enough to do these things, too.

718
00:45:49,700 --> 00:45:53,800
而思考如何把流程和验收标准写清楚
And figuring out how to write down the processes and the acceptance criteria becomes the

719
00:45:53,800 --> 00:45:57,180
就成了这份工作里用智能体做元编程的那一部分
metaprogramming part of the job, using these agents.

720
00:45:57,680 --> 00:45:58,920
这是一个非常好的收尾方式
That's a great way to end it.

721
00:45:58,960 --> 00:45:59,780
多么令人兴奋的特性
What an exciting feature.

722
00:46:00,160 --> 00:46:01,900
大家把掌声送给瑞安，谢谢各位
Give it up for Ryan, guys. Thank you, folks.
